cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI/ML-Based Solar Photovoltaic Power Forecasting: A Reproducible and Explainable Benchmark Across Forecast Horizons and Weather Conditions"
message: >-
  If you use this software, the experiment configuration or the results in this
  repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kapoor
    given-names: Pratham
    email: prathamkapoor027@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrathamKapoor/solar-pv-forecasting"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
keywords:
  - solar photovoltaic
  - power forecasting
  - time series forecasting
  - machine learning
  - deep learning
  - explainable AI
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  A controlled, leakage-audited benchmark of classical machine learning,
  recurrent, hybrid and attention-based models for short-term solar photovoltaic
  power forecasting, evaluated across four forecast horizons, four weather
  regimes, four seasons, feature-group ablations, statistical significance tests,
  permutation and SHAP explainability, conformal prediction intervals and
  computational cost.
